course: dictionary
lesson: 13754
title: Intermediary: the go-between
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: An intermediary is a person or group who stands between two sides. They help those sides talk, agree or make a deal. «Tom and Ava had fallen out, so their teacher acted as an intermediary.» The teacher did not take a side. She carried messages and helped them find an agreement.
explain: Another word for an intermediary is a go-between. «The two countries sent their messages through an intermediary.» The intermediary passed words from one country to the other, so they could talk without meeting face to face.
explain: Intermediary can also be an adjective in formal writing. It means in the middle, between two stages or things. «The intermediary stage of the project was the hardest part.» Here it means the middle step, between the start and the finish.
fact: An intermediary is a person or group who goes between two sides.
fact: «Intermediary» is a noun, and its plural is «intermediaries».
fact: In conflict, a teacher or a peer mediator can act as an intermediary between pupils who have fallen out.
fact: In news, countries use intermediaries to help end wars or free hostages.
fact: In business, an intermediary connects buyers and sellers.
exercise: In «Ava and Leo fell out, so Mrs Khan acted as an intermediary», what is Mrs Khan? | *A go-between who helps them agree | The thing they argued about | A player in the game they were playing | A new pupil in the class
exercise: What is another word for intermediary? | A rival | A judge who always picks a winner | A spectator | *A go-between
exercise: «The intermediary stage of the project was the middle step.» What does intermediary mean here? | *In the middle, between two stages | At the very end | Very loud | Something that is broken
test: «Countries sent messages through an intermediary to end the war.» Why did they need an intermediary? | To start a fight | To pick a winner | To hide the messages from everyone | *To pass messages and help them talk
test: Which sentence uses intermediary as a noun? | Ben ran intermediary fast. | *Our intermediary helped the buyer and seller agree a price. | The intermediary stage took three weeks.
exam: What does «act as an intermediary» mean? | To fight on one side | To run the fastest race | *To stand between two sides and help them agree | To sell the most toys
